{
    "background_story": "Esme was a small, unassuming weevil with a big appetite for grains. As a member of the Sitophilus genus, she was part of a long line of pantry pests. But Esme was different - she had a passion for history and preservation. While her fellow weevils were content to simply eat and reproduce, Esme spent her days burrowing through ancient grain stores, uncovering forgotten knowledge and hidden treasures. She was particularly fascinated by the art of grain storage, and spent countless hours studying the techniques of ancient civilizations. Despite her tiny size, Esme's love of learning and her unique perspective on the world made her a beloved figure among the insect community.",
